HST Office: Slides' theme gallery shows 6, 4 or 3 themes in a row on Windows and macOS too, as on Linux.

The gallery narrows with the ribbon state (hst-ribbon-ux-gallery-fit.patch) by sizing the .ui's scrolled window
"hstthemescroll". That window exists with the GTK builder only: the vcl builder (Windows, macOS, Qt, headless)
drops a scrolled window whose child scrolls by itself (VclBuilder::cleanupWidgetOwnScrolling), so
weld_scrolled_window() returned nothing there and the gallery kept the .ui's 680 px, about 6 themes, at every
ribbon state: at 1366 px Thiết kế folded "Chủ đề ▾" where Linux shows 4 themes. Without the scrolled window the
icon view itself is sized: as many of its own item widths as the state's columns, plus the frame and scroll bar;
the vcl icon view lays out as many columns as that width holds.

License: the edited upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); the new test file is HST-owned (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary).
